# rule.always.weigh-each-claim-with-one-burden

> **hold every claim to one burden of proof, whichever way it points. a skeptic who doubts only what it dislikes is a dogmatist with good tools.**

the order of the reads starts with your own claim; the burden of each is the same.
uneven looks like: the claim you like passes on one read, the rival owes three · a peer's claim read, yours on recall · "fixed" relayed, "regressed" re-run twice · flaws hunted on one side only.
test: **would this read have moved me as far if it had pointed the other way?**
blocker: a claim you favor accepted on less proof than its rival was asked for, and acted on by a peer
nitpick: a review that hunts flaws in one side only
